 "requested_at": "2026-11-13T20:08:34.672827Z",
 "text": "Under the *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006* (RTA), a landlord has the statutory right to enter a rental unit to carry out repairs, replacements, or work. \n\nSection 27(1), paragraph 1 permits a landlord to enter the rental unit upon providing at least 24 hours' written notice \"[t]o carry out a repair or replacement or do work in the rental unit.\" Section 27(2) stipulates that the written notice must specify the reason for entry, the day of entry, and a time of entry between the hours of 8:00 a.m. and 8:00 p.m. Landlords are also permitted to be accompanied by contractors or other agents to perform the work. Because the clause mirrors and complies with these statutory entry provisions, it is valid and enforceable.\n\nVerdict: enforceable\nSection: 27",
